    <!-- Round 265: the home page's canonical, in the template rather than in
         the app. Every OTHER page carries one because the prerenderer captures
         the head after React has drawn it, but the home page is deliberately
         not prerendered (the host regenerates it every build), so its canonical
         only existed once JavaScript ran. Measured on the live site with
         JavaScript off and a Googlebot user agent: ten pages checked, ten
         canonicals, and the one that was missing was the home page. It is also
         the page most likely to collect tracking parameters from shares, which
         is exactly what a self referencing canonical is for. -->
    

    <!-- Round 281: who this site is, in the template rather than at runtime.

         Every other page ships as a snapshot whose head is copied verbatim from
         the build, so a tag React adds survives. The home page is the one page
         that cannot work that way, because vite regenerates it from THIS file on
         whatever machine builds the site, so anything added at runtime never
         reaches the raw HTML. Measured on 2026-08-24, the shipped home page
         carried zero structured data blocks: the WebApplication object the app
         has been generating since Round 53 had never been seen by a crawler,
         only by a browser that runs JavaScript. Same trap that swallowed the
         canonical in Round 265 and the readable copy in Round 257.

         WebSite and Organization are the two things Google reads to work out
         whose domain this is and what to call it, and WebApplication is what
         says the thing at this address is a free browser game rather than a
         shop or a blog. All three are claims about the SITE rather than about
         whichever page is being served, and each carries an @id naming the site
         root so none of them can be read as a claim about the current page.
         Putting them here does exactly that: the snapshots copy this head, so
         all 126 of them carry the pair and a crawler can tie 127 documents to
         one entity. The page level object, whatever type that page is, is still
         emitted by PageSeo on top of this.

         KEEP THIS IN STEP WITH SITE_JSON_LD in src/lib/pageSchema.ts.
         scripts/simSchema.mjs parses this block and compares it against that
         export, so the two cannot drift apart quietly. -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://douknowball.com/#website","name":"DoUKnowBall","alternateName":"Do U Know Ball","url":"https://douknowball.com/","inLanguage":"en","publisher":{"@id":"https://douknowball.com/#org"}},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","@id":"https://douknowball.com/#org","name":"DoUKnowBall","url":"https://douknowball.com/","logo":"https://douknowball.com/icon-512.png"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebApplication","@id":"https://douknowball.com/#webapp","name":"DoUKnowBall","url":"https://douknowball.com/","applicationCategory":"GameApplication","operatingSystem":"Web Browser","isAccessibleForFree":true,"offers":{"@type":"Offer","price":"0","priceCurrency":"USD"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://douknowball.com/#org"}}]</script><script type="application/ld+json" data-rh="true">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"DoUKnowBall","item":"https://douknowball.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Soccer Games","item":"https://douknowball.com/soccer"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Soccer Career","item":"https://douknowball.com/soccer-career"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json" data-rh="true">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I save my career?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Automatically, in your browser, after every decision. There is one career per browser, and starting fresh permanently deletes the old save. An optional account adds site stats and leaderboards, but the career lives on your device."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I win the Ballon d'Or?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Post the best season in the world and the voters have to give it to you. If you outscore every player on the shortlist and win a league, Champions League, or World Cup, you win it outright, and any season of 45 goals or 55 goal involvements finishes top 3 at worst. Trophies still decide the close years, and a second place finish becomes next season's fuel."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens after retirement?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Four paths: read your legacy breakdown and walk away, farm controversy as a TV pundit, chase trophies as a manager, or buy a club that is up for sale and run it as owner."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the highest legacy score?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"100, with GOAT starting at 90. Expect to need multiple Ballon d'Ors and Champions Leagues, a World Cup, huge totals, and a clean record, since one scandal can separate GOAT from LEGEND."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I play for the club I came through as a youth player?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The senior side of your academy club always puts a contract on the table when you turn pro, usually on slightly lower wages because they know you would sign for free. Staying gives you a popularity and morale boost and unlocks the homegrown legend storylines. From 27 they can also call you back for a homecoming transfer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is corruption mode and can it end my career?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is the dirty half of the game and yes, it absolutely can. Taking envelopes from a betting syndicate, paying a referee's brother in law, buying Ballon d'Or votes, or laundering cash through your own nightclub all raise a hidden heat meter. Stay hot too long and you get raided, then convicted, then you serve a season in prison while your stats rot. There is always a way out: confess, take the tax amnesty, or just stop, and heat cools every clean season."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this a football career sim game or a management game?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A career sim first: you steer one player's life and story, not tactics. The manager and owner modes afterward add a taste of the other side."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Soccer Career free to play?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Soccer Career is free to play on DoUKnowBall, right in your browser. No download and no signup needed."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json" data-rh="true">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Game","name":"Soccer Career: Free Football Career Simulator | DoUKnowBall","description":"Start at 16 in a youth academy and live a whole soccer career: transfers, trophies, feuds, scandals and a legacy verdict. A free football life sim game.","url":"https://douknowball.com/soccer-career","isAccessibleForFree":true,"gamePlatform":"Web Browser","publisher":{"@id":"https://douknowball.com/#org"}}</script>
    
    
