<h1>⚽ Soccer Career</h1>
<p>Create your player. Build your legend.</p>
<h2>Create Your Player</h2>
<h2>Create Your Look</h2>
<p>The volume seller. Red, loud, everywhere.</p>
<p>Your career saves in this browser. No account needed.</p>
<h2>Soccer Career: Free Football Career Simulator</h2>
<p>Live out your soccer dream in a season by season career simulator. Create a player, join a youth academy, develop skills, sign contracts, win trophies, and compete for the Ballon d'Or.</p>
<p>Every soccer career simulator promises the same fantasy: start as a nobody, retire as a legend. This one makes the middle the good part. You begin at 16 in a youth academy and live season by season through contracts, transfers, injuries, feuds, trophies, and increasingly questionable purchases, until the game hands down a legacy verdict. For scouting and development, try <a href="/wonderkid-factory">Wonderkid Factory</a>.</p>
<p>It is the most played game on DoUKnowBall, and it sits closer to a life sim than to a match engine. You never dribble anyone. You make decisions, and the sim turns them into a story that is different every run. Compare offers as the agent in <a href="/contract-chaos">Contract Chaos</a>.</p>
<p>Your save lives in your browser, one career at a time, so choices carry weight into the years that follow them.</p>
<p>You build your player's actual face before kickoff: skin tone, hairstyle and colour, facial hair, a boot line, an accessory, and a signature celebration that gets described every time you score. That look follows you onto the Ballon d'Or stage and into your retirement send off.</p>
<p>There is a dirty side too. Bent officials, betting syndicates, kickbacks, offshore accounts and laundering fronts all sit there waiting, each one heating up a hidden investigation meter. Take enough envelopes and the dawn raid comes, then the trial, then a season inside and a comeback from nothing.</p>
<h2>How to play Soccer Career, a free football career simulation game</h2>
<h3>Creating your player and building your look</h3>
<li>Create your player: name, one of 50 nationalities, one of 10 positions, and a starting era from the 1990s to the 2020s.</li>
<li>Build your look in the appearance editor: 12 skin tones, 29 hairstyles, 16 hair colours, 18 beard styles, 16 accessories, 18 boot lines, and 19 signature celebrations, or hit Surprise me.</li>
<h3>Rolling potential and customizing your build</h3>
<li>Roll your starting potential, somewhere in the mid 50s to high 60s, and reroll as many times as you like. Rerolls are free and there is no limit on them.</li>
<li>Open Customize your build to set your starting overall anywhere from 40 to 99, move points between the six attribute families, shape the specifics under each family, and set your height and weight.</li>
<h3>Starting in the academy and turning pro</h3>
<li>Begin in an academy matched to your nationality and talent. Pro contract offers arrive from age 17.</li>
<h3>Advancing seasons through the training ground</h3>
<li>Advance season by season through simulated stats, newspaper headlines, random events, and decisions.</li>
<li>Most summers open with one card about your position or your career, before the rest of the news between seasons. Training can trade one skill for another next season, with gains stopping at your ceiling.</li>
<li>Want to see it happen? The 📺 Week by week button plays the same season match by match, with your rating every game and the league table after every matchday, then hands you back to the newspaper. Its ? button has the rules and worked examples.</li>
<li>Up to three times a season the clock stops and the moment is yours to play on your training ground board (look for 🎯 on the fixtures): a YOUR CALL decides how that match went, with the return game taking the other side so your final table and season totals never move, and a RECREATE replays what the record says you did, for stars that bank into next season's growth.</li>
<li>Open the training ground (the dumbbell button, above your player on phones or bottom right on desktop) once a season. Your position picks a drill you actually play: keepers hold and drag a glove save dive, centre backs, full backs and defensive midfielders time a tackle on a moving ball, central and attacking midfielders thread a through ball onto a runner before he is offside, and everyone else times a wall shot through a gap that opens and closes. Today's ten rounds are the same for everyone at your position and count once; practice is unlimited and banks nothing.</li>
<h3>Working transfer windows and the shop aisles</h3>
<li>Work the transfer windows: stay, extend, request a move, or weigh rival offers and dream club pay cuts.</li>
<li>When the window offers it, open Set transfer priority, choose minutes, club level or home country, save the brief, then use Request transfer. Saving the brief alone does not request a move, and No Agent can use it too.</li>
<li>After a settled senior season, open Review representation to compare agent terms or choose No Agent before a later deal.</li>
<li>Spend the money in 8 shop aisles: property, vehicles, investments, lifestyle, performance, flex, family, and a shady aisle that only appears once you have something to hide.</li>
<h4>Retiring into management, punditry or ownership</h4>
<li>Retire, on your terms or your body's, collect the legacy verdict, then carry on as a manager, pundit, or owner if you want.</li>
<li>Want one last year? Eligible players from 30 can open Plan a farewell season, read the terms and confirm their final year. You can still choose to retire immediately.</li>
<li>If you previously retired from internationals, an eligible National-team comeback lets you make yourself available again after a settled season.</li>
<h2>Soccer Career rules: growth, legacy and the corruption meter</h2>
<h3>How stats grow through your prime</h3>
<li>Stats grow slowly and honestly: 1 to 3 points a year through the academy and your prime, less once you pass 86, and barely at all above 90. Reaching world class is a decade of work, not three good seasons.</li>
<li>Growth fades once your hidden prime type (early, normal, late, or extended) ends, with decline turning brutal from 38.</li>
<h3>Your boyhood club and retirement age</h3>
<li>The club that raised you always offers you a first team deal when you turn pro, so you can spend a whole career at your boyhood club, and it can call you home again from 27.</li>
<li>Retirement is suggested from age 30 once you drop 10 off your peak or hit 75 overall, forced below 50 overall at 33 or older, and automatic at 45.</li>
<li>From 30, renewal and transfer pay follow your age, overall and latest playing season. A renewal or extension lasts two years at 30 to 33, then one from 34. Another club keeps the years shown on its offer.</li>
<li>A money talk still has a 50% chance of success. From 30, success raises or holds your current wage; it does not renew the contract.</li>
<li>A farewell is one declared final year for eligible players aged 30 to 44. The announcement is saved and cannot be undone or extended. Finish its results and queued ceremonies, then retire. Injuries, bans and forced retirement still apply; appearances and trophies are not promised.</li>
<h3>The World Cup cycle and your legacy score</h3>
<li>The World Cup comes every 4 years. Top nations qualify about 90 percent of the time, while a small nation mostly needs a world class you.</li>
<li>After international retirement, eligible players aged 18 to 44 with a recorded cap can return once per recorded season. Existing caps, goals, trophies and history stay the same. Returning opens selection, not an instant call-up or extra caps; injury, bans and failed qualification can still keep you out.</li>
<li>Legacy runs 0 to 100: 90 is GOAT, 80 LEGEND, 70 GREAT, 60 SOLID PRO, and less is JOURNEYMAN. The verdict also knows the overall you started at, so climbing from 54 to 91 scores better than being handed 91 on the creation screen.</li>
<h3>Starting overall and your growth ceiling</h3>
<li>There is no cap on your starting overall, but a high start eats the room you had to grow into, and if you are already world class as a teenager you pick up far more injuries before you turn 24.</li>
<li>Your ceiling is not welded shut. Two seasons in a row that are both elite and decorated, while you are already pressed against it, buy one point back at a time. 99 is the hard wall and nothing gets past it.</li>
<h4>How a position drill trains your attributes</h4>
<li>A position drill is ten rounds and its session score is wins times ten. 50 pays +1 to the drill's attribute with next season's growth (shooting for the wall shot, defending for the tackle, passing for the through ball, reflexes for the glove save) and 80 pays +2, capped at the room between your overall and your ceiling, so a drill never lifts you past it. It shares the one training session a season with the cone slalom, sprint burst, passing gates and penalty sessions.</li>
<h3>Physical stats, morale and integrity</h3>
<li>Height and weight are real numbers, not decoration: a tall heavy player wins more in the air and is stronger, and is slower off the mark and less agile for it.</li>
<li>Morale runs 0 to 100, moves with events and choices, and counts: 89 and up adds a league game and a tenth on your rating, 73 and under costs the same, 58 and under two of each, never more than three games together with the dressing room. Scandals feed an integrity ledger worth minus 30 to plus 20 legacy points at the end.</li>
<h4>A pay cut, an injury and a rival's Ballon d'Or</h4>
<li>A statistically dominant season cannot be snubbed at the Ballon d'Or. Outscore the whole shortlist while winning a major and the trophy is yours, and any 45 goal or 55 goal involvement season finishes on the podium at worst.</li>
<li>After a settled senior season, ages 19 to 44 can change representation once per recorded season. Agents and No Agent affect future signings and income fees; your current wage, savings and already-paid fees stay the same.</li>
<li>A transfer priority searches the clubs already eligible for your age and rating. The usual response chance is 50%; a broken appearance promise guarantees a response, but not an offer. The response is saved for that window and cannot be rerolled by reloading. Projected minutes are not guaranteed starts, and club-arranged sales and loans keep their own flow.</li>
<h4>Corruption heat and dirty money</h4>
<li>Corruption heat runs 0 to 100 and cools 8 a year when you stay clean. Past 70 the financial crimes unit can raid you, and past 90 comes a conviction, seized money, and a season in prison that wrecks your stats.</li>
<li>Unexplained money keeps generating heat every season until you wash it through a shady business or declare it and eat the tax.</li>
<h3>Derby days against your club's rivals</h3>
<li>Derbies: if your club has a real rival in the same league, you meet them twice a season in the league. We only count a rivalry two separate sources back, in leagues and years where we checked how often the clubs meet, so some clubs have none yet.</li>
<li>You play the derbies you are picked for, roughly in line with your league appearances. Each one you win adds 2 popularity and 2 morale, each one you lose takes 2 off both, a draw changes nothing, the swing is capped every season and your rating is never touched.</li>
<li>Score the goal that puts you ahead for good in a derby win and the season counts as a Derby Hero season, worth 2 more popularity. Example: at Arsenal you beat Tottenham 2-1 at home with the winner and draw 1-1 away, so that is +4 popularity, +2 morale and a Derby Hero.</li>
<h3>Your domestic cup run</h3>
<li>Every season your club plays its country's domestic cup as a run, from the early rounds to the final, and the cup carries its real name (the FA Cup, the Copa del Rey, the DFB-Pokal) wherever two sources back it; a cup that was not played that season cannot be won.</li>
<li>Go out early and your season summary names the round and the club that knocked you out. Win it and the celebration walks you through the run, and your trophy chip names the cup.</li>
<h2>Soccer Career walkthrough: a striker's rise to a Ballon d'Or revenge arc</h2>
<h3>A Nigerian striker breaks out as a teenager</h3>
<p>Take a Nigerian striker rolled at 63, a Gifted start. Two academy years push him past 70, and at 18 a bidding war breaks out. He takes minutes over money, bags 20 league goals, and the papers crown him the next superstar.</p>
<h3>A dream transfer and a torn hamstring</h3>
<p>At 22 a dream club calls with a pay cut, and he signs anyway. A league title lands in year two, then a torn hamstring eats half a season, and a moral dilemma offers a shady shortcut back to fitness. He refuses, banking integrity, while the rival the game spawned at his debut, a preening Brazilian winger, lifts the Ballon d'Or. The snub becomes fuel.</p>
<p>A separate pay example: with No Agent, at 35 and 76 overall after a playing season rated 7.1, a €1,000 base offer is quoted at €850 a week. Another club keeps the years shown on its offer. If the current wage is €1,000, a successful pay talk holds it at €1,000 instead of cutting it, without renewing the contract.</p>
<h3>A revenge arc ends in LEGEND tier retirement</h3>
<p>The revenge arc peaks at 26: a Champions League, a World Cup semifinal carrying Nigeria, then the Ballon d'Or, where he thanks the rival from the stage. An extended prime runs to 36, the fortune buys his boyhood club, and he retires at 38 with a legacy of 84, LEGEND tier, one Champions League short of GOAT talk.</p>
<h2>Soccer Career tips for growing stats and building your legacy</h2>
<h3>Rerolling your potential before you start</h3>
<li>Reroll your potential to 62 or better. The gap between a Promising start and a Gifted one echoes for a decade.</li>
<h3>Training sessions and steering growth events</h3>
<li>The training ground is the dumbbell button, one session a season. The older sessions (cone slalom, sprint burst, passing gates, penalties or shot stopping) pay +1 at 50 and +2 at 80; the position drill pays the same but stops at your ceiling. Beyond that, growth follows your age curve, and you steer it through event choices, lifestyle purchases, and the social media detox, worth plus 2 to every stat next season.</li>
<li>In goal the same drills train keeper skills: the cone slalom is footwork and pays Positioning, the sprint burst pays Sweeping Speed, the passing gates pay Distribution and shot stopping pays Reflexes. Outfield players train Dribbling, Pace, Passing and Shooting from the same four tiles.</li>
<h3>Paying for a trainer and the recovery clinic</h3>
<li>Money matters: a personal trainer adds a stat point per season, and the recovery clinic halves injury layoffs.</li>
<h3>Weighing the doping risk, your agent and loyalty</h3>
<li>The doping storyline boosts every stat but risks a 20 percent failed test each season it runs, and failing means a 1 season ban and a wrecked reputation.</li>
<li>Your personality and representation shape the whole run. The Showman grows followers 60 percent faster, The Professor earns brand trust, and super agent Zara Blackwood opens dream club doors for a 10 percent cut.</li>
<li>Loyalty pays: a decade at one club is worth about as much legacy as two and a half league titles.</li>
<h2>Soccer Career FAQ: saves, the Ballon d'Or and corruption mode</h2>
<h3>How do I save my career?</h3>
<p>Automatically, in your browser, after every decision. There is one career per browser, and starting fresh permanently deletes the old save. An optional account adds site stats and leaderboards, but the career lives on your device.</p>
<h3>How do I win the Ballon d'Or?</h3>
<p>Post the best season in the world and the voters have to give it to you. If you outscore every player on the shortlist and win a league, Champions League, or World Cup, you win it outright, and any season of 45 goals or 55 goal involvements finishes top 3 at worst. Trophies still decide the close years, and a second place finish becomes next season's fuel.</p>
<h3>What happens after retirement?</h3>
<p>Four paths: read your legacy breakdown and walk away, farm controversy as a TV pundit, chase trophies as a manager, or buy a club that is up for sale and run it as owner.</p>
<h3>What is the highest legacy score?</h3>
<p>100, with GOAT starting at 90. Expect to need multiple Ballon d'Ors and Champions Leagues, a World Cup, huge totals, and a clean record, since one scandal can separate GOAT from LEGEND.</p>
<h3>Can I play for the club I came through as a youth player?</h3>
<p>Yes. The senior side of your academy club always puts a contract on the table when you turn pro, usually on slightly lower wages because they know you would sign for free. Staying gives you a popularity and morale boost and unlocks the homegrown legend storylines. From 27 they can also call you back for a homecoming transfer.</p>
<h3>What is corruption mode and can it end my career?</h3>
<p>It is the dirty half of the game and yes, it absolutely can. Taking envelopes from a betting syndicate, paying a referee's brother in law, buying Ballon d'Or votes, or laundering cash through your own nightclub all raise a hidden heat meter. Stay hot too long and you get raided, then convicted, then you serve a season in prison while your stats rot. There is always a way out: confess, take the tax amnesty, or just stop, and heat cools every clean season.</p>
<h3>Is this a football career sim game or a management game?</h3>
<p>A career sim first: you steer one player's life and story, not tactics. The manager and owner modes afterward add a taste of the other side.</p>
<h3>Is Soccer Career free to play?</h3>
<p>Yes. Soccer Career is free to play on DoUKnowBall, right in your browser. No download and no signup needed.</p>
